% The pigeonhole again, but reached by PROPAGATION rather than by the declarations, and
% therefore the case where M4-T1's `pol` goes decorative.
%
% a + b >= 7 and c + d >= 7 over 1..4 force all four variables into 3..4, so [3, 4] is a
% Hall interval holding four variables and two values. Unlike alldiff_hall_unsat, every
% one of those bounds MOVED, so each at-least-one line has to be narrowed and the Hall
% derivation carries the four bound literals into its row. Cancelling them needs "the id
% of the line that establishes this bound fact", which Explanation.t cannot say (D-0009's
% open ADT gap), so lib/core/prop/alldiff.ml cancels them with Explanation.clause instead
% -- the claim index hands back the trace line that already states each one, minting
% nothing -- and Search.rests_on_a_clause then closes the root the D-0022 way.
%
% So `conclusion UNSAT` here cites `rup >= 1`, not the Hall pol: the derivation is still
% checked (it is on the page, and the empty clause is RUP only because it is), but it is
% not what the conclusion rests on. alldiff_hall_unsat is the model that shows the other
% case, and the pair is the evidence M4-T1 was asked for. test/unit/test_prop.ml asserts
% both citations, so neither is a claim about output nobody reads.
var 1..4: a :: output_var;
var 1..4: b :: output_var;
var 1..4: c :: output_var;
var 1..4: d :: output_var;
constraint int_lin_le([-1,-1],[a,b],-7);
constraint int_lin_le([-1,-1],[c,d],-7);
constraint all_different_int([a, b, c, d]);
solve satisfy;
